{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1111488-input-needed-on-houseruling-heroes","id":1111488,"title":"Input needed on houseruling Heroes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-04T18:45:37-07:00","id":1111488,"title":"Input needed on houseruling Heroes","content":"So I had an idea about tweaking Heroes to bring them closer to their legendary roots and make them more versatile in the ways they conflict with Beasts: Those Heroes would be superhumanly talented people with inflated egos and ambitions, whose supernatural abilities don't work on normal humans unless they're fueled by enery gained by thwarting Beasts' feedings, and furthermore, the Heroes could only gain new abilities by taking trophies from the Beasts they've decisively defeated (meaning either killing them, imprisoning them, driving them off or otherwise removing the Beast from the area for good). To those Heroes, fighting Beasts would by default be a mean to an end, Beasts being a source of power and glory, which the Heroes need to reach their true goals.<br /> <br /> For example; a Hero wanting to become Mayor of a town would save a cheating husband from a Nemesis to fuel her or his supernatural charisma, or kill the Nemesis outright and take her eyes as a trophy, to gain the ability to become invisible to spy on her or his rival for the mayor seat.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't prevent some Heroes from being fanatics obsesssed with killing Beasts, picky slashers, or righteous defenders against the Begotten menace, but it would allow for more nuance and diversity in their antagonism, I think?<br /> <br /> I'm mostly wondering about the mechanics: should those Heroes have their own Supernatural resistance stat? A modified, Satiety-like Integrity? Should they use willpower as fuel for their abilities? Should the trophies allow the Heroes to buy Atavisms possessed by the Beast they come from to allow stuff like Perseus gaining Medusa's head, or should I just keep heroic Gifts?<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T18:54:33-07:00","id":1111493,"title":"","content":"I believe you will find good inspiration in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/846783-homebrew-beast-merits\"><b>this</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/847546-hero-the-quest-new-template\"><b>this</b></a> thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:33:27-07:00","id":1111502,"title":"","content":"Thanks! The Trophy Gift actually solves one of my problems nicely!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":